--
--  GF(2^8) arithmetic over the primitive polynomial 0x11D
--  (x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1) -- the standard choice for Reed-Solomon.
--
--  The tables are FROZEN CONSTANTS, generated and verified offline (inverses,
--  associativity, distributivity) and pasted here.  They are not built at
--  elaboration: a literal table has no elaboration order to reason about, no
--  initialisation loop to prove, and it can be read and checked by a human.
--  This is the same discipline the soliton table uses in gnat-lt-pro.
--
--  Addition in GF(2^8) IS exclusive-or; there is no carry and no overflow.
--  That is why this whole unit is trivially free of run-time errors: every
--  operation is a table lookup or an xor, and every index is bounded by
--  construction (see Mul).

